   "text": "The drawing is a cucurbituril macrocycle. I counted 14 carbonyl oxygens, which means 7 glycoluril units, so this is cucurbit[7]uril, C42H42N28O14. Adjacent glycoluril units are joined by two CH2 bridges, one at each portal, and the 7 units close into a ring. No wedges or hashes are drawn, so I included no stereochemistry.\n\nI built the SMILES as seven glycoluril fragments written separated by dots. Each fragment has a top carbonyl ring and a bottom carbonyl ring that share the CH\u2013CH bond. The CH2 bridges between neighbouring units, and the seventh-to-first closure, are made with ring-closure labels (%11\u2013%17 for the top bridges, %21\u2013%27 for the bottom bridges).\n\nI did not run this through a SMILES parser. I checked by hand that every ring-closure label is opened once and closed once, and that the atom counts match C42H42N28O14.\n\nSMILES: N1%17C(=O)N(C%11)C2C1N%27C(=O)N2C%21.N1%11C(=O)N(C%12)C2C1N%21C(=O)N2C%22.N1%12C(=O)N(C%13)C2C1N%22C(=O)N2C%23.N1%13C(=O)N(C%14)C2C1N%23C(=O)N2C%24.N1%14C(=O)N(C%15)C2C1N%24C(=O)N2C%25.N1%15C(=O)N(C%16)C2C1N%25C(=O)N2C%26.N1%16C(=O)N(C%17)C2C1N%26C(=O)N2C%27"
